id: pm-vcs-0lec
title: Add sparse lazy instances with a shared immutable object store
description: "Materialize per-instance views over complete repository trees, fetch missing fragments lazily, and let independent working trees share immutable objects while retaining separate HEAD index view dirty state and operation logs."
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-08-01T19:32:33.737Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-16T03:33:27.951Z"
assignee: pi-agent
claim_principal: pi-agent
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 1800
acceptance_criteria: A sparse view never changes committed tree identity and merges evaluate the complete tree; Out-of-view conflicts and incomplete PM attribution fail visibly rather than disappearing; Concurrent instances share immutable objects but cannot overwrite one another mutable state; A full scan reconciles dirty hints and filesystem state without trusting hints as authority
parent: pm-vcs-b7cb
risk: high
comments[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-15T22:52:46.319Z",pi-agent,"Starting implementation. Design: sparse linked instances over the hub's shared immutable store. Per-instance control directory holds HEAD, index (v4 with a sparse flag, git skip-worktree style), oplog, view.json, dirty-hint file and merge state; the hub keeps objects, refs, config and remotes shared (refs protected by existing compare-and-swap locks). Sparse index entries keep out-of-view content in every committed tree so a view can never change tree identity and merges always evaluate complete trees. Missing objects surface as typed missing_fragment errors with fetch remediation. Dirty hints are hints only: they can force extra verification, never suppress it; the full scan rewrites them from filesystem truth."
  "2026-08-16T03:33:27.951Z",pi-agent,"Regression proofs: each mutation was applied to the shipped code, its covering test observed failing (exit non-zero), and the mutation reverted; the full suite re-ran green after each revert. (1) materialize() drops sparse index entries -> 'a sparse view never changes committed tree identity' FAILS. (2) merge materializes out-of-view conflicts instead of refusing (outOfView forced empty) -> 'an out-of-view conflict fails visibly' FAILS. (3) commit accepts staged out-of-view changes (guard disabled) -> 'committing a staged change outside the view is refused' FAILS. (4) SharedObjectStore rethrows object_not_found untranslated -> 'a missing fragment is a typed, actionable error' FAILS. (5) instances open private stores/refs instead of the hub's -> concurrency test FAILS (shared store missing). (6) RefStore ignores headRoot so instances share HEAD -> concurrency test FAILS (HEAD overwritten). (7) scan() returns hinted paths instead of verified ones -> 'a full scan reconciles lying hints' FAILS. (8) status() stops passing hints as forced content checks -> the racy-stat adversarial case inside 'a full scan reconciles lying hints' FAILS (the forged-stat edit reads clean without the hint)."
body: ""
